Changes in Moka: ONNX Runtime backend (CPU / optional CUDA, TensorRT, OpenVINO),
export-only PyTorch graph targeting ONNX instead of Core ML, dynamic-axis
input handling, Linux RAPL energy sampling, INT8 dynamic quantization as an
opt-in approximate variant, and a Linux CI fidelity gate.

The model follows Laya's DecisionModel and Hugging Face Transformers ModernBERT.
Original checkpoint weights belong to their respective upstream authors and are
downloaded separately. No Hub weights are included in this repository.

Moka is an independent community port, not an official release of Convai
Innovations, laya-coreml, laya-mlx, Microsoft ONNX Runtime, or Intel OpenVINO.
